              "a11yCheck": "Check the answers. The responses will be marked as correct, incorrect, or unanswered.",
              "a11yShowSolution": "Show the solution. The task will be marked with its correct solution.",
              "a11yRetry": "Retry the task. Reset all responses and start the task over again.",
              "textField": "While the statins have many positive health benefits, they are contraindicated in pregnancy, being a *pregnancy category D* drug. They are also contraindicated in *liver disease*. The statins cannot be combined with other lipid lowering agents such as vitamin B3, also known as *nicotinic acid* or the *fibrates* because all of those agents have a slight risk of causing rhabdomyolysis which is a rapid muscle breakdown that is extremely toxic and can cause acute *kidney failure*, but if combined, those drugs have a high risk of the disorder. One thing that they can be combined with is ezetimibe, which is the medication that decreases cholesterol absorption from the GIT."
